ose left column is an object color and right column is its halo color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:14:    - Away from the markers, every source color from the legend appears as one or more 4-connected monochrome objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:15:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:16:    Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:17:    - Keep the input pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:18:    - For each source-color object, take its tight bbox expanded by one cell and clipped to the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:19:    - Recolor background pixels in that expanded region to the marker's halo color, except for background holes enclosed by the object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:20:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:21:    Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:22:    - The small left-edge bars are a legend: they map object colors to the colors used for the surrounding padded bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:23:    \"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:24:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:25:    bg = int(get_bg(g))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:26:    out = g.copy()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:27:    h, w = g.shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:28:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:29:    markers: dict[int, int] = {}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:30:    marker_source_cells: dict[int, set[tuple[int, int]]] = {}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:31:    for comp in find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=False, return_format=\"dict\"):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5adee1b2.py:32:        r0, c0, r1, c1 = comp[\"bbox\"]\n/home/li